From 8b2e3583322bad27f5c5294aca0a0746f3bfea30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jahidul Hossain Mekat <jahidulhossainmekat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:11:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Collect the queue statistics only on the steps that are
 logged

StatsLogger._collect computed the number of pending, running and chunked
requests on every step, but they only end up in the log line, which is written
every DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP steps. They are not free:
get_sum_prompt_len_waiting and get_sum_prompt_len_chunked each walk the whole
waiting queue, a pointer chase per sequence, which takes 0.13 ms together at 10k
waiting sequences and 1.9 ms at 100k, on every step of an engine that has
statistics enabled (the default for the engine, not for LLM).

Compute them with the other statistics that are only needed on logging steps.
log_step already requires those to be free of side effects.
